From 9e50a1ee2739ee189fad239816cdb96c68a45852 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhenyu Li <zhl136@ucsd.edu>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:56:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] A verdict is fail-closed on the rows its session carries

ADMITTED says "the focused prefix reproduced and the flip took the other
arm".  That is a claim about the SESSION -- the rows EXPLORE and COMPOSE
read -- and `FocusedReplay.results` decided it from `FLIPPED` alone, which
is process state that outlives the rows.  HDFS-17960 on 39bedd768, session
`793875fb482a10a4-4b39d011`: a 0-byte `roots.jsonl`, no `seq=79` decision,
a `TASK_UNANSWERED REPLAY_PREFIX_UNMATCHED: the focused occurrence did not
take the decision its obligation flips:` in its own `gaps.jsonl` -- and
`obligations-0000/793875fb482a10a4/obligation_result.jsonl` reading
ADMITTED, which X17 R4b's rule then carries into the composition as a
disjunct.  The 42 rows of the abandoned occurrence, the root mint among
them, are simply not in the corpus.

One rule, in the one account of what a replay settled, and it only ever
REFUSES an admission -- every other verdict keeps the words it had:

* a prefix this replay was ABANDONED on.  An abandoned occurrence
  publishes nothing, so the session loses its whole row set.
  `ConcolicResultPublisher.taskUnanswered` is the one door every
  unanswered-task gap goes through and its detail opens with the reason it
  documents, so `FocusedReplay.noteUnansweredTask` keeps the
  REPLAY_PREFIX_UNMATCHED ones and ignores the rest; the gap is the
  verdict's stated reason.
* a root the wave assigns whose MINT ROW the session does not state.  Told
  apart from `planted` on purpose: the plant writes the field and survives
  an occurrence whose rows are then discarded, while `mintPublished` --
  filed by `RowRuntime.rootMint` right where the row is published -- says
  the SESSION states the mint.  Over both spellings of what a wave asks of
  a root, an absolute assignment and a clock's skew, for the reason
  `unplantedAssignments` gives.

Against the two corpora this is written about: the refused run's
`cb67875d1d896d4d-73ab772f` states its mint row and no prefix gap, so it
stays ADMITTED; `793875fb482a10a4-4b39d011` has neither and states
NOT_ADMITTED.  Pass #8's two focused sessions both state
`roots.jsonl seq=121` and neither carries a prefix gap, so both stay
ADMITTED.

Folded into `aMintStatesTheValueItRead`, which already drives the flip at
the obligation's own occurrence over 17960's shape: the flip alone is now
NOT_ADMITTED naming the roots whose rows are missing (the clock's skew
among them), each mint row admitted in turn, and a prefix gap un-admits
what was admitted.  46 @Test, shell test green.

